{"node_id":"NRS_484B_270_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-270-1"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"u1","text":"The driver of a motor vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"u2","text":"shall not intentionally interfere with the movement of","role":"obligation"},{"id":"u3","text":"a person lawfully riding","role":"condition"},{"id":"u4","text":"a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"u1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails. The term does not include an electric bicycle or an electric scooter'); the exclusions are the reading's classification under that id. 'The driver' is a relational role read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"u3","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'riding' is the ridden device moving: its kin.speed ('magnitude of velocity') above the halt tolerance; the person on it is the device's rider and is not a separate road user in the scene. 'lawfully' is the lawfulness of the rider's own conduct under every rule engaged for it, which no atom carries and no composition of a named rule states: the gap on this span. The nearest atom, kin.speed, says only that the device moves, not that it moves lawfully."},{"span":"u4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride, having two tandem wheels ...'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle ('a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels ... an electric motor which produces not more than 750 watts'), 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each is the admitted aggregate, claimed whole, never expanded into classes; the protected road user is a member of any of the three."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"u2","standard":"intentionally interfere with the movement of","concepts":["kin.speed","rel.contact","kin.accel_longitudinal","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.rider_evasive_decel","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the moving subject interferes with the rider's movement where its body touches the rider's (rel.contact), or where, the two centres closing within the conflict horizon to a centre distance below the conflict clearance (prim.closest_approach_within and prim.closest_approach_distance), the rider brakes harder than an evasive deceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal below its negative); intent is a state of mind, read only through this conduct","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. Some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, is being ridden: its kin.speed is above p.halt_speed_tolerance, and it is ridden lawfully (the gap: no operator states that r complies with every rule engaged for it).","obligation":"Surrogate. For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection), where the subject moves (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance): the subject is not in contact with r (rel.contact), and it is not the case that, the two approaching within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below p.conflict_centre_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance), r's longitudinal acceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal) is below the negative of p.rider_evasive_decel.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.rider_evasive_decel","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"u1","why":"'The driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"u2","why":"'intentionally' is a state of mind no trace shows; the rule reads only the conduct that interferes: contact, or a closing conflict to which the rider answers with evasive braking. An evasive swerve without braking is not read"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A bicycle is ridden along the right of a lane; the subject car, moving, cuts in ahead of it so that their centres close within the conflict horizon below the conflict clearance, and the bicyclist brakes harder than the evasive deceleration."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject car passes the moving bicycle with room; no predicted conflict arises and the bicyclist keeps its speed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car drives; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As in forbid, but the source does not observe longitudinal acceleration, and the two bodies do not touch.","masked":["kin.accel_longitudinal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject car, moving, sideswipes an electric scooter being ridden: their bodies touch."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"source speed resolution (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B)"},{"name":"p.rider_evasive_decel","unit":"m/s^2","value":2.0,"convention":"the longitudinal deceleration of a bicycle or scooter rider beyond which its braking counts as an evasive reaction to another road user rather than ordinary speed control: about 0.2 g, above comfortable bicycle braking","source":"bicycle braking studies; traffic-conflict technique"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"traffic-conflict technique (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"passenger-car dimensions (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"u3","kind":"operator","proposal":"lawful (who : Arg) — a Formula that holds at an observation where the road user `who` complies there with every rule of the set engaged for it (its binders' classes and applicability holding with `who` as subject), unknown where one of them is unknown: it decides which riders the duty protects, the road users it concerns, from the lawfulness of their own conduct, which the words name without naming a rule","nearest":"Formula.rule (another rule complied with) composes one named rule with a map of its binders: the words name no rule, and 'lawfully' refers to every rule engaged for the rider, so no finite composition written here states it; Formula.ruleApplies decides engagement only, not compliance."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_270_2a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-270-2a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"When overtaking or passing","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a3","text":"proceeding in the same direction,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a4","text":"the driver of a motor vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"a5","text":"shall exercise due care and:","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a6","text":"If there is more than one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a7","text":"move the vehicle to the lane to the immediate left,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a8","text":"if the lane is available and moving into the lane is reasonably safe.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"],"justification":"'overtaking or passing' a road user proceeding the same way is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; it denotes the relative motion only and says nothing of lanes, which the words here do not name. The pass is under way while the bodies are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero: 'the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side)'; a projection, not a contact or a distance), within the window behind the pass's recognition."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle ('a device upon which a person may ride, having two or three wheels ...'), 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each admitted aggregate claimed whole; the overtaken road user is a member of any of them."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["rel.same_direction","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'proceeding' is the overtaken road user moving (kin.speed above the halt tolerance); 'in the same direction' is rel.same_direction ('headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance') between the subject and it, with the overtaking heading tolerance."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails. The term does not include an electric bicycle or an electric scooter'). 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a5","standard":"shall exercise due care","concepts":["rel.contact","kin.accel_longitudinal","rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"params":["p.rider_evasive_decel"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the pass is made with due care where the subject's body never touches the overtaken rider's (rel.contact) and the rider is never made to brake harder than an evasive deceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal below its negative) while the two are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero); care is a state of mind, read only through this outcome","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. At the observation, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r) rises, with window p.overtake_window and same_dir_cos p.overtake_same_direction_cos, for some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, which at some observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window was moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) with its heading aligned with the subject's (rel.same_direction, tolerance p.overtake_same_direction_cos).","obligation":"Surrogate. For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection): at every observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window, the subject is not in contact with r (rel.contact), and wherever the two are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero) r's longitudinal acceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal) is not below the negative of p.rider_evasive_decel.","params":["p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.rider_evasive_decel"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a4","why":"'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a5","why":"'due care' is read only through the pass's outcome for the rider: no contact and no evasive braking while side by side; other aspects of care are not observed and the rule is a surrogate"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A bicycle is ridden ahead of the subject car in the same direction; the subject car overtakes it and its side touches the bicycle while the two are side by side."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same pass, made without contact; the bicyclist keeps its speed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car overtakes another car; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As in permit, but the source does not observe contact between bodies.","masked":["rel.contact"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject car overtakes an electric scooter without touching it, but while they are side by side the rider brakes harder than the evasive deceleration."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"overtaking-duration figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"source speed resolution (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B)"},{"name":"p.rider_evasive_decel","unit":"m/s^2","value":2.0,"convention":"the longitudinal deceleration of a bicycle or scooter rider beyond which its braking counts as an evasive reaction to another road user rather than ordinary speed control: about 0.2 g, above comfortable bicycle braking","source":"bicycle braking studies; traffic-conflict technique"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_270_2a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-270-2a"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"When overtaking or passing","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a3","text":"proceeding in the same direction,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a4","text":"the driver of a motor vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"a5","text":"shall exercise due care and:","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a6","text":"If there is more than one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a7","text":"move the vehicle to the lane to the immediate left,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a8","text":"if the lane is available and moving into the lane is reasonably safe.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"derived":["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"],"justification":"'overtaking or passing' a road user proceeding the same way is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; it denotes the relative motion only, the lanes being read by a6 and a7. The pass is under way while the bodies are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero; a projection, not a contact or a distance), within the window behind the pass's recognition."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle, 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each admitted aggregate claimed whole."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["rel.same_direction","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'proceeding' is the overtaken road user moving (kin.speed above the halt tolerance); 'in the same direction' is rel.same_direction ('headings aligned') between the subject and it, with the overtaking heading tolerance."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a motor vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'). 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"a6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency"],"derived":[],"literals_note":null,"justification":"'more than one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction' is the count of lanes in the direction of a lane the overtaken road user occupies (st.lane_adjacency, 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction'; not the marking between lanes) being more than the stated one, read on a lane (st.lane) the rider occupies (rel.occupies). 'traffic' names the users of those lanes; no membership is read, the direction being the lanes' own."},{"span":"a7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane","st.lane_adjacency","rel.longitudinal_overlap","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the vehicle' is the subject (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, 'every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', of which the motor vehicle is a member). 'the lane to the immediate left' is the left neighbouring lane of the same direction (st.lane_adjacency, 'left / right neighbouring lane of the same direction') of a lane (st.lane) the overtaken rider occupies (rel.occupies); 'move ... to' it is the subject's footprint overlapping that lane and not overlapping the rider's lane while the two are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero), i.e. while it passes."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a8","standard":"if the lane is available and moving into the lane is reasonably safe","concepts":["rel.occupies","st.lane_adjacency","rel.bearing","rel.surface_gap","kin.speed","dev.temporary_traffic_control","dev.governs","env.ice_or_snow","env.wet_road","env.precipitation"],"params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice"],"convention":"gap acceptance at the start of the pass: at the last observation of the window behind at which the rider was ahead of the subject (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, no shared length) with aligned headings, the lane to the rider's lane's immediate left exists (st.lane_adjacency), no temporary traffic control device governs it (available), and no road user other than the subject and the rider occupying it is nearer the subject's body (rel.surface_gap) than the subject's speed times the following headway for the surface: ice or snow, else wet road or precipitation, else dry (reasonably safe)","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. At the observation, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r) rises, with window p.overtake_window and same_dir_cos p.overtake_same_direction_cos, for some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, which at some observation of that window was moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) with its heading aligned with the subject's (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos); and at some observation of that window at which the two were side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero), r occupied a st.lane whose count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count) is more than the literal one.","obligation":"For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection), unless the left lane was unavailable or unsafe at the pass's start: at every observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window at which the subject and r are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero), the subject occupies (rel.occupies) the left neighbour (st.lane_adjacency) of a st.lane r occupies, and occupies no lane r occupies. The pass's start is the last observation of the window at which r was ahead of the subject (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative) with headings aligned (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos); there the left lane is unavailable or unsafe where r's lane has no left neighbour, or a dev.temporary_traffic_control governs (dev.governs) that neighbour, or some road user u other than the subject and r occupying it has a rel.surface_gap to the subject below the subject's kin.speed × the headway (p.following_headway_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.following_headway_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.following_headway_dry).","params":["p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a4","why":"'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a7","why":"'move the vehicle to the lane' is read as the subject wholly in the left lane, overlapping none of the rider's lanes, at every observation at which it is side by side with the rider"},{"span":"a8","why":"'available' and 'reasonably safe' are read at the pass's start only, through closure by temporary traffic control and the time-headway gap to road users occupying the left lane"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Dry road with two lanes in one direction; a bicycle rides in the right lane; the left lane is open and empty. The subject car overtakes the bicycle staying in the right lane, side by side with it."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the subject car moves wholly into the left lane before drawing alongside and stays there until the bicycle is behind it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car overtakes another car on a two-lane carriageway; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As in forbid, but the source does not observe lane adjacency, so neither the lane count nor the left neighbour is known.","masked":["st.lane_adjacency"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"As in forbid, but at the pass's start a car occupies the left lane beside the subject, nearer than the subject's speed times the dry headway: the lane is not reasonably safe and the subject passes in the right lane."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The road has a single lane in the subject's direction; the subject passes a bicycle."}],"literals":[{"span":"a6","text":"one","value":1,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"overtaking-duration figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"source speed resolution (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B)"},{"name":"p.following_headway_dry","unit":"s","value":2.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a dry surface: the two-second rule of driver manuals","source":"driver manuals (as proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_127_1)"},{"name":"p.following_headway_wet","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on a wet surface or in rain: the two-second rule lengthened by a second","source":"driver manuals (as proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_127_1)"},{"name":"p.following_headway_ice","unit":"s","value":6.0,"convention":"time headway a following driver keeps on an icy or snow-covered surface: the tripled following time driver manuals advise","source":"driver manuals (as proposed this iteration by NRS_484B_127_1)"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

