nalizations":[{"span":"a8","standard":"if the lane is available and moving into the lane is reasonably safe","concepts":["rel.occupies","st.lane_adjacency","rel.bearing","rel.surface_gap","kin.speed","dev.temporary_traffic_control","dev.governs","env.ice_or_snow","env.wet_road","env.precipitation"],"params":["p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice"],"convention":"gap acceptance at the start of the pass: at the last observation of the window behind at which the rider was ahead of the subject (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, no shared length) with aligned headings, the lane to the rider's lane's immediate left exists (st.lane_adjacency), no temporary traffic control device governs it (available), and no road user other than the subject and the rider occupying it is nearer the subject's body (rel.surface_gap) than the subject's speed times the following headway for the surface: ice or snow, else wet road or precipitation, else dry (reasonably safe)","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. At the observation, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r) rises, with window p.overtake_window and same_dir_cos p.overtake_same_direction_cos, for some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, which at some observation of that window was moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) with its heading aligned with the subject's (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos); and at some observation of that window at which the two were side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero), r occupied a st.lane whose count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count) is more than the literal one.","obligation":"For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection), unless the left lane was unavailable or unsafe at the pass's start: at every observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window at which the subject and r are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero), the subject occupies (rel.occupies) the left neighbour (st.lane_adjacency) of a st.lane r occupies, and occupies no lane r occupies. The pass's start is the last observation of the window at which r was ahead of the subject (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative) with headings aligned (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos); there the left lane is unavailable or unsafe where r's lane has no left neighbour, or a dev.temporary_traffic_control governs (dev.governs) that neighbour, or some road user u other than the subject and r occupying it has a rel.surface_gap to the subject below the subject's kin.speed × the headway (p.following_headway_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.following_headway_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.following_headway_dry).","params":["p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a4","why":"'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a7","why":"'move the vehicle to the lane' is read as the subject wholly in the left lane, overlapping none of the rider's lanes, at every observation at which it is side by side with the rider"},{"span":"a8","why":"'available' and 'reasonably safe' are read at the pass's start only, through closure by temporary traffic control and the time-headway gap to road users occupying the left lane"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Dry road with two lanes in one direction; a bicycle rides in the right lane; the left lane is open and empty. The subject car overtakes the bicycle staying in the right lane, side by side with it."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the subject car moves wholly into the left lane before drawing alongside and stays there until the bicycle is behind it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car overtakes another car on a two-lane carriageway; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As in forbid, but the source does not observe lane adjacency, so neither the lane count nor the left neighbour is known.","masked":["st.lane_adjacency"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"As in forbid, but at the pass's start a car occupies the left lane beside the subject, nearer than the subject's speed times the dry headway: the lane is not reasonably safe and the subject passes in the right lane."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The road has a single lane in the subject's direction; the subject passes a bicycle."}],"literals":[{"span":"a6","text":"one","value":1,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.overtake_window","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind","source":"overtaking-duration figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.overtake_same_direction_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.9,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other","source":"lane-change heading figures (as proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_30_030)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: 