ane.heading_right_of_carrier(subject, L) with sin_tol p.course_departure_sin_tol and speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance holds for no st.lane L that r occupies (rel.occupies).","params":["p.overtake_window","p.overtake_same_direction_cos","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.course_departure_sin_tol","p.following_headway_dry","p.following_headway_wet","p.following_headway_ice"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b4","why":"'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"b9","why":"'move again to the right side of the highway' is read as the subject's heading turned to the right of the rider's lane direction beyond the course tolerance, after it has the rider on its right; a gradual drift within that tolerance is not read"},{"span":"b10","why":"'safely clear' is read as the rider behind the subject at a time-headway gap at the rider's speed; the rider's own braking ability is not otherwise read"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Road with one lane in the subject's direction; the subject car moves out left and overtakes a bicycle; while the bicycle is still beside it, the subject car steers back to the right, its heading turning right of the lane's direction beyond the course tolerance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same pass; the subject car keeps its course until the bicycle is behind it at a gap above the bicycle's speed times the dry headway, then steers back right."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject car overtakes another car on a one-lane road and steers back; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As in forbid, but the source does not observe headings.","masked":["kin.heading"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject car completes the pass of an electric scooter and s